WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.140
- I have to bring this up

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.400
'cause I think it's funny.
- Okay.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.660
- You were in another club.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.430
I was in this club too, Girl Scouts.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.263
You're a Brownie?

00:00:06.263 --> 00:00:07.290
- I was kind of one.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.810
- Okay, but I heard that
(chuckles) you got kicked out.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.002
- Yeah, so I think when-
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:12.960
(audience laughing)
- Who gets kicked out?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.164
- Only the coolest people, obviously.

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:15.870
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.800
Well, I was little,

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.000
so you're only like five or six

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.710
in Brownies.
- When you're brownies, yeah.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.330
- And so I don't think
they officially call it

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.163
just kicked out,

00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:23.910
they're not that hardcore.
- Hardcore.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.442
You're just not welcome back. (laughs)

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:26.490
(audience laughs)
- But me and my best friend,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.530
Jamie Valentine, in Arizona,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.150
I think we were just
being too rambunctious,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.160
and I think the story on the street

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.460
is that they told our moms
that we weren't invited back.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.810
- Oh, my gosh.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:37.680
- We weren't Brownie material.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.513
I don't know what to say.

00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:39.947
We loved it.
- Aah.

00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:41.428
- I hold it dear,

00:00:41.428 --> 00:00:42.300
I think that's pretty cool.
- I got kicked outta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.680
Sunday school once.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.690
- What'd you do?
(audience laughs)

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.590
- Here's the thing.
(audience laughs)

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.125
My friend, Mary, whatever,

00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:52.410
(Keri laughs)
my friend, Mary, and I, we,

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.460
I was like, I don't know
if I should say this,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.320
but we were laughing at something else.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.760
- It happens.
- In the Sunday school,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:57.720
and you know, when you're a kid-

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.700
- And you can't stop.
- You just can't stop.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.990
- Can't stop.
- In the Sunday school,

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.090
the teacher was very sensitive

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.701
in the first place.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.990
- And probably shouldn't have been

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.301
a youth leader in general.
- A youth leader, yeah.

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.760
(audience laughs)
- This was not her forte.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.980
- No.
- And so we laughed,

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.030
and then we tried to stop.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.290
Like, I'm so respectful,

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.670
but I could not stop laughing,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.503
and then we got kicked out.
- It makes it worse.

00:01:18.503 --> 00:01:20.070
- And then I was like, oh, my God,

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.986
who gets kicked out of
Sunday school? (laughs)

00:01:21.986 --> 00:01:23.250
(audience laughs)
- Cool people.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.240
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.650
- I was like, I know I felt bad.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.850
I think about her to this day.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:27.690
I feel bad about it,

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.990
but I, once you start
laughing, it's hard to stop.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.280
- It's such a good release though.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.113
- And then you-
- And those are so,

00:01:33.113 --> 00:01:34.110
it's amazing.
- Exactly,

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.760
and then you're like,
you're laughing even more

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.200
'cause you're supposed to stop,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.735
and you're a jerk.

00:01:38.735 --> 00:01:39.720
You're in puberty.
- It's culture chaffing.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.734
- You're already a jerk already.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.120
- Yup.
- Like, it's, yeah,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.270
it was not a good time.

